# oraclia-language

## Oraclia · symbolic language in development

Oraclia is an experimental symbolic language and relational reading system currently in development.

It works with an alphabet of 21 symbols understood as operators rather than words with fixed meanings.

The project explores how a situation or conversation can be read through symbolic fields, relations, forms and transformations, and how these configurations may change over time.

The symbols are not intended to define a person or impose a fixed interpretation. Every reading is provisional and can be corrected or rejected.

When there is not enough structure to support a symbolic configuration, Oraclia can preserve that indeterminacy instead of forcing an interpretation.

The project is currently in a prototyping and experimental phase.

